ATTRIBUTION TO ORIGINAL HYPERMAIL
==================================

This software is inspired by and maintains configuration compatibility
with the original Hypermail email archiver.

Original Hypermail:
  Copyright (C) 1994 Enterprise Integration Technologies Corp. (EIT)
  Copyright (C) The Hypermail contributors
  Licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later
  Project page: https://www.hypermail-project.org/

Original Hypermail Authors and Maintainers:
  - Tom Gruber - Original Lisp prototype at EIT (1994)
  - Kevin Hughes - C rewrite and initial maintainer at EIT
  - Kent Landfield - Primary maintainer through versions 2.0-2.4
  - Daniel Stenberg - MIME multipart, RFC 2047, trio library integration
  - Peter McCluskey - Lead developer; linkquotes, folder_by_date, threading
  - Jose Kahan, Stian Soiland, Jim Meyering - Major contributors
  - and other contributors

Hypermail-rs is a complete Rust rewrite with no original C code. It adds modern
features while maintaining the spirit and configuration compatibility of the original.
We are deeply grateful to the original Hypermail team for creating such a useful
tool for the open-source community.

